---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Mila Business Solutions LLC"
  description="What happens to a query you paste into the SQL Performance Review, what we store, and what we don't."
>
  <Section narrow>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="margin-top:var(--space-3);">What happens to what you paste</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        The SQL Performance Review asks strangers to paste potentially sensitive
        business data into a text box. That deserves a straight answer rather
        than a policy nobody reads. Last updated {updated}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow tight>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Your query is sent to an AI provider to produce the review, and is not
        stored by us. The provider route is configured to retain nothing. We
        keep a one-way hash of your IP address for 48 hours purely to enforce
        rate limits. Please still redact anything genuinely confidential —
        the safest data is the data you never send.
      </p>

      <h2>The SQL Performance Review</h2>

      <h3>What gets sent</h3>
      <p>
        Exactly what you put in the two boxes: the query, and the schema/index
        definitions if you supply them. Plus which database dialect you picked.
        Nothing else — no cookies, no account, no browsing history.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bear in mind what a query can carry: table and column names, database
        and schema names, and any literal values in a <code>WHERE</code> clause —
        which can include customer names, email addresses, IDs, or dates.
        <strong>Replace real literals with placeholders before pasting.</strong>
        The review is just as accurate with <code>WHERE email = 'x@example.com'</code>
        as with a real address.
      </p>

      <h3>Where it goes</h3>
      <p>
        The request is sent to <a href="https://openrouter.ai" rel="noopener">OpenRouter</a>,
        which routes it to a model provider. Routing is constrained to providers
        that support zero data retention and have training/data collection
        denied. If no provider currently meets those conditions, the request is
        refused rather than quietly routed somewhere weaker — you'll see an
        error instead of a review.
      </p>

      <h3>What we store</h3>
      <p>
        Of the review itself: nothing. The query, the schema, and the generated
        response are not written to any database or log. They exist only for the
        seconds it takes to produce your result.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do store one thing: a <strong>keyed hash of your IP address</strong>
        with a timestamp, so the free demo can enforce its per-visitor and daily
        limits. The hash is one-way and computed with a secret key, so the
        original address cannot be recovered from it. These rows are deleted
        automatically after 48 hours.
      </p>

      <h3>What we log</h3>
      <p>
        Error logs record that a failure happened and its category. They do not
        record your query, your schema, request bodies, or request headers.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        Whatever you type into it — typically a name, an email address, and a
        description of your problem — is stored in our database so we can reply.
        It isn't sold, shared, or used for marketing lists. Ask us and we'll
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no tracking cookies and runs no third-party analytics.
        The only thing stored in your browser is your light/dark theme
        preference, which never leaves your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions or deletion requests</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:admin@milabiz.com">admin@milabiz.com</a>, or use
        the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. If you'd like the contact
        record deleted, say so and it will be.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this changes materially — particularly anything about what is sent to
        a third party or what is retained — the date at the top changes with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--c-fg-muted);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--c-fg);
  }
</style>
